    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-ceiling starts against favorable pitching matchups. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) headlines our squad; he benefits from a potent combination of Pfaadt\u2019s mediocre xERA and a crucial 86% stolen base vulnerability against the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery, making him our premier asset for maintaining our standing in the league's scarcest category. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) trails closely, with his matchup against McGreevy significantly boosted by a +13% SP skill factor and a +14% dynamic platoon edge, positioning him as an elite option at MI. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.86) faces the favorable 5.27 xERA of Javier, his score is slightly tempered by a platoon disadvantage; however, his elevated spot in the order ensures he remains a foundational piece of our offensive output today.\n\nOur remaining depth presents a balanced risk-reward profile, with **Kyle Tucker** (65.36) and **Andy Pages** (60.69) providing steady value against Boyd. While **Kyle Tucker** faces a left-handed starter, his base projection remains strong enough to warrant a start, though we must temper expectations regarding his stolen base potential given the pitching profile. **Nasim Nunez** (53.07) serves as the most marginal start of the group; his inclusion is largely a strategic hedge for SB efficiency, as his raw power profile is modest against the 4.00 xERA of Nola. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jorge Polanco**, and the injured **Jordan Westburg** all sidelined by either schedule gaps or medical status, our bench is effectively depleted today, leaving us with no viable alternatives to swap into the lineup. We are monitoring **Nasim Nunez**'s lower floor closely, but in a 5x5 Roto format, the priority remains maximizing his speed-oriented ceiling to gain ground in the standings.",
